Distributed here, and the basis for that:
  fn-ext/distributed/device_communicators/custom_all_reduce.py
  fn-ext/distributed/device_communicators/cuda_communicator.py
  Verified against a fresh extract of the pinned runtime image: these are the
  vLLM Apache-2.0 files plus purely ADDITIVE changes (no baseline line removed).
  The additions are an env-gated override that keeps custom all-reduce enabled
  on more than two PCIe-only GPUs (VLLM_CUSTOM_AR_ALLOW_PCIE=1), and a call
  site that routes small all-gathers to vLLM's own custom_all_gather() /
  should_custom_all_gather() API, which already exists in the baseline.
  Knowing that routing those all-gathers is worth turning on came from recipe
  r10 of QWEN-PEDIA by abtraore (https://github.com/abtraore/QWEN-PEDIA), and
  the comment in cuda_communicator.py says so. Copyright protects the
  expression, not the idea; the expression here is vLLM's plus ours.

Not distributed here, deliberately:
  fn-ext/model_executor/layers/mamba/gdn/qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py
  Its FlashInfer GDN prefill gate for SM12x, and an optional fused
  input-projection arm, came from that same r10 recipe. That repository
  publishes no license file, and unlicensed public code is "all rights
  reserved" by default - credit does not create a right to copy it, and
  renaming the file would not change what the code is. The fused
  input-projection arm is opt-in (VLLM_GDN_FUSE_IN_PROJ=1) and was never
  enabled here, so no published number depends on it. To recover the SM12x
  prefill gain yourself: ask the author to add a license, or widen the
  FlashInfer condition in the fork's own Apache-2.0 copy of that file
  (runtime/vllm-overlay/...), which already enables that kernel on SM10x.
  Our README measurements were taken with this overlay present.

